{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cdd5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1834e-5c30-7891-bc12-a51ead89f1ec"},"sequence":1349,"recorded_at":1780531400002693,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1834e-5e54-7173-a07b-84d0dcd98bd2","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1834e-5e54-7173-a07b-84d0dcd98bd2","event":{"chunk":"edited\nchanged lines: line 19\n--- original\n+++ updated\n@@\n-4. **Skin is read once.** `useState(skinTreatment)` reads `data-skin` only on mount. Watch `html[data-skin]` with a MutationObserver so a skin switch restyles the mark live. Martin's rule is to pick by data-skin whenever it is available, with engraving as the default.\n+4. **Skin is read once.** `useState(skinTreatment)` reads `data-skin` only on mount. Watch `html[data-skin]` with a MutationObserver so a skin switch restyles the mark live. Martin's rule is to pick by data-skin whenever it is available, with engraving as the default.\n+\n+## Fixes (round 1)\n+\n+1. **Auto page-turn.** The tick read `span` (plus `enabled`/`manifest`) from the effect closure while the deps list never re-ran it for a new scene under a kept chapter manifest, so the voice gated against the previous scene's span. Every input now comes from `live.current` each tick, and the gate is the pure `autoTurnTarget()` in `app/narration/turn.ts`, covered with real `paginateScene` pages. Lookup and `textPage` both run in text-page space and `onTurnPage` re-adds the cover shift, so the indices line up. Nothing stamps `lastManualRef` on mount or on the Read aloud click (only pager and figure moves do) — but the stamps used `Date.now()` while the gate reads `performance.now()`, so after any hand move the 8 s window never elapsed; both stamps now use `performance.now()`. Next scene and next chapter advance is the narration controller's `timeupdate`/`ended` handoff across the full scene order; the live-inputs fix keeps the follow loop alive across it.\n+2. **Chapter cover.** `syncEnabled` no longer requires `kind === \"text\"`, so the loop runs on the cover (and end page): with no container the mark stays clear, and the first active chunk auto-turns onto its text page through the same manual-window gate. The measure effect also re-runs on text-page change so the mark paints right after a turn.\n+3. **Engraving mark.** Dropped `letter-spacing: 0.04em` from `.narr-word`; the overlay measures its natural width and shrinks with `transform: scaleX()` (origin left) via pure `engravingScale()`, tested, so it never covers neighbouring characters and never stretches. Colours still come from tokens; no new icons.\n+4. **Skin.** `useReadSync` watches `html[data-skin]` with a `MutationObserver` and restyles the mark live on switch. The pick rule is unchanged: data-skin whenever available, engraving as the default.\n","final_result":true,"kind":"output","task_id":"01a18356-346c-7a83-a446-7fb2d4f0db09"},"kind":"task_lifecycle","run_stream":{"id":"01a1834e-5e54-7173-a07b-84d0dcd98bd2","kind":"run"},"task_id":"01a18356-346c-7a83-a446-7fb2d4f0db09","task_stream":{"id":"01a18356-346c-7a83-a446-7fb2d4f0db09","kind":"task"}}}
