{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000cfbf","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a1834e-5c30-7891-bc12-a51ead89f1ec"},"sequence":1594,"recorded_at":1780531400003183,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"01a1834e-5e54-7173-a07b-84d0dcd98bd2","payload_type":"run.terminal.completed","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"command_id":"01a1834e-5e54-7173-a07b-84d0dcd98bd2","kind":"run_terminal","reason":null,"run_stream":{"id":"01a1834e-5e54-7173-a07b-84d0dcd98bd2","kind":"run"},"terminal":"completed","text":"All four findings are fixed, documented, and committed as [9cb015e](https://example.com/commit/9cb015e), [dee4887](https://example.com/commit/dee4887), [6c13a67](https://example.com/commit/6c13a67), [4ea3402](https://example.com/commit/4ea3402) plus the \"Fixes (round 1)\" section in [docs/reviews/41.md](/workspace/wt-41/docs/reviews/41.md).\n\n- Auto-turn: the tick now reads every input from `live.current` each tick (the closed-over `span` gated the voice against the previous scene), the gate is the pure `autoTurnTarget()` in [turn.ts](/workspace/wt-41/app/narration/turn.ts) tested with real `paginateScene` pages, and both manual stamps use `performance.now()` — they used `Date.now()` while the gate reads `performance.now()`, so one hand move pinned auto-turn shut forever.\n- Cover: the loop runs on every sub-page kind, turning onto the first text page through the same manual-window gate.\n- Engraving: letter-spacing dropped, overlay shrinks via `scaleX(min(1, w/natural))`, origin left, through tested `engravingScale()`; tokens-only colours, no new icons.\n- Skin: a `MutationObserver` on `html[data-skin]` restyles the mark live; pick rule unchanged.\n\nGates: 573 tests pass, `tsc`, `check:size`, `check:secrets` clean; the single failing file is the known pre-existing Node 20 `pipeline/ingest.test.ts` infra failure, identical on the untouched base.\n\nSkipped live-browser verification (no `next dev`/`start` per your rules), and I did not add a DOM-level test for the observer or the scale measurement — jsdom has no layout, so the pure-helper tests are the honest coverage there."}}
